~ deal

if GameState.has_flag("reach_done")
	Fence: Rig's east. Told you — gate's open. Don't die where I can see it, it's bad for trade.
	=> END
Fence: You walk like a man following somebody. And the only somebody worth following through here went east, toward the rig.
Fence: I know the gate schedule. I know which pens are counted and which aren't. That's worth something.
Liris: He sells passage through his own employer's fence.
Fence: I sell *certainty*, warden. The Extractors sell holes in the world. One of us is honest about it.
Fence: So. My price: whatever the Menders were paying you to carry. Or walk the long way and count the pens yourself while the harvest runs.
- Pay him and move fast
	Sarro: Done. The trail's cold enough already.
	Fence: Pleasure. East gate, third pen — it's blind after the shift bell.
	Fence: The one you're following — grey coat, cartographer's case. He didn't haggle either.
	Liris: (quietly) Every hour that rig runs, something on the other side goes thinner.
	do GameState.set_flag("reach_done")
	do GameState.set_flag("fence_deal")
	do GameState.grant_xp(2500)
- Refuse — we take the long way [Liris]
	Liris: We don't fund this place. Not even in passing.
	Fence: Principles. Expensive things out here.
	Sarro: We'll manage.
	Fence: You will, at that. Tell you what — watching the pair of you argue with a fence line will be entertainment enough. Gate's mispatrolled at the far corner. Free of charge.
	Fence: Grey coat. Cartographer's case. East. Now we're square, and you owe me nothing.
	do GameState.set_flag("reach_done")
	do GameState.add_conviction(1)
	do GameState.grant_xp(2500)
=> END
